[00:06.76] A winter's day
[00:11.51] In a deep and dark December
[00:15.87] 
[00:19.67] I am alone
[00:24.23] Gazing from my window to the streets below
[00:28.08] On a freshly fallen silent shroud of snow
[00:31.51] I am a rock I am an island
[00:34.61] 
[00:44.74] I've built walls
[00:49.02] A fortress deep and mighty
[00:52.19] 
[00:55.51] That none may penetrate
[01:00.46] I have no need of friendship, friendship causes pain
[01:05.06] It's laughter and it's loving I disdain
[01:08.45] I am a rock I am an island
[01:14.47] 
[01:21.31] Don't talk of love
[01:25.67] Well I've heard the word before
[01:28.72] 
[01:32.22] It's sleeping in my memory
[01:34.82] 
[01:37.49] I won't disturb the slumber of feelings that have died
[01:41.63] If I never loved I never would have cried
[01:45.22] I am a rock I am an island
[01:48.08] 
[01:58.37] I have my books
[02:02.39] And my poetry to protect me
[02:08.80] I am shielded in my armor
[02:14.81] Hiding in my room safe within my womb
[02:18.32] I touch no one and no one touches me
[02:22.02] I am a rock I am an island
[02:25.03] 
[02:31.10] And a rock feels no pain
[02:34.59] And an island never cries
[02:35.63] 